    {
      "id": "claim_41c075a307a840558b82aed661c445a4",
      "statement": "populateUI in JS.html evaluates user state in a strict, non-commutative cascade where the first matching branch wins and short-circuits the rest: (1) Withdrawal_Count >= 3 -> Locked (state 6); (2) isOnProbation -> Probation (state 7); (3) isCoolingDown -> Cooldown (states 3, 8); (4) isEnrolled (non-blank Current_Plan) -> Enrolled (states 2, 5, 10); (5) default -> Eligible (states 1, 4, 9). The enrolled/eligible branches also show the enrollment attempt number as withdrawalCount + 1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Profile.gs#L99-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bbe5ec148efb588f3abddff1530b127ae841daaa2f14666bd7c17d2720fccecf:"
        },
        {
